lamss3 is distributed under two licenses:

| Code                                                | License                    | Text           |
|-----------------------------------------------------|----------------------------|----------------|
| Libraries (`<toolbox>/src/lib/`)                    | LGPL-3.0-or-later          | COPYING.LESSER |
| Applications, scripts, missions, everything else    | GPL-3.0-or-later           | COPYING        |
| Third-party code (`<toolbox>/src/thirdparty/<name>`)| as stated in that directory| (its own file) |

Each source file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier header naming its license.
Where that header differs from the table, the header wins: a library that links
GPL code (such as MOOS-IvP) is GPL-3.0-or-later.
Submodule toolboxes (mit, icex, attic, hydroman/upstream, user toolboxes)
carry their own license terms.
